# Copy to .env and fill in. Never commit the filled-in file (.gitignore lists .env).
#
# WHAT MAY LIVE IN THIS FILE: DAYTONA_API_KEY and OPENROUTER_API_KEY. The drivers read
# each from the environment, else from this file (scripts/daytona/daytona_lib*.py,
# scripts/tau3_cc/openrouter_key.py; for the Daytona key, EVOSKILL_ENV_FILE names another file).
#
# WHAT MUST BE EXPORTED IN THE SHELL: the Claude Code credential. `evoskill run` reads it
# from the process environment only (src/orchestrator/cc_account.py), never from this
# file. In the shell that starts the run, export ONE of
#
#   export EVOSKILL_CC_TOKEN_FILE=/path/to/token_file   # `claude setup-token` saved to a
#                                                       # file with mode 600 (the path only)
#   export ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=...                        # used only when no token file is given
#
# (or pass --token-file). With a token file, ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is removed from every Claude
# Code session's environment, so a key left in the shell never moves a token-file run onto
# API billing. The same credential serves the solver, the evolver and the adaptor.

# --- Daytona (every run) ---
DAYTONA_API_KEY=

# --- tau3 runs only: the simulated customer and the knowledge-base search ---
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# The dataset is given on the command line (`evoskill run --data DIR`); no variable is needed.
